  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "TRIAL EDITION - SQL longer than 10,000 characters is rejected (parse() returns -1). Full edition: https://www.sqlparser.com\n\nRelease 4.1.0.16\n\n- [DB2] Recognize the event monitor statements SET EVENT MONITOR\n  ... STATE, CREATE EVENT MONITOR and ALTER EVENT MONITOR ... ADD\n  LOGICAL GROUP. For example, SET EVENT MONITOR m STATE 0 and\n  CREATE EVENT MONITOR m FOR ACTIVITIES WRITE TO TABLE ACTIVITY,\n  ACTIVITYSTMT (IN USERSPACE1 PCTDEACTIVATE 100) MANUALSTART\n  previously failed to parse. Like other Db2 administrative\n  statements, they are returned as TUnknownSqlStatement with\n  sqlstatementtype set to sstdb2seteventmonitorstate,\n  sstdb2createeventmonitor or the new sstdb2altereventmonitor.\n\nDemos: https://github.com/sqlparser/gsp_demo_dotnet",
